1
00:00:00,06 --> 00:00:02,02
- [Narrator] Being a React developer means

2
00:00:02,02 --> 00:00:03,01
that you should know

3
00:00:03,01 --> 00:00:05,07
about good software design and architecture.

4
00:00:05,07 --> 00:00:07,01
As a React developer,

5
00:00:07,01 --> 00:00:09,00
your responsibilities are to design

6
00:00:09,00 --> 00:00:12,00
and implement the UI components of a web application

7
00:00:12,00 --> 00:00:14,05
by using good software practices.

8
00:00:14,05 --> 00:00:17,00
And your job is to provide and deliver clean code

9
00:00:17,00 --> 00:00:19,03
that is maintainable and scalable.

10
00:00:19,03 --> 00:00:20,05
As easy as it sounds,

11
00:00:20,05 --> 00:00:22,07
being a good React developer requires

12
00:00:22,07 --> 00:00:26,07
expertise in many areas, such as project organization,

13
00:00:26,07 --> 00:00:29,00
software testing and quality assurance,

14
00:00:29,00 --> 00:00:31,01
performance and optimization,

15
00:00:31,01 --> 00:00:33,05
and also state management.

16
00:00:33,05 --> 00:00:35,03
What is state management?

17
00:00:35,03 --> 00:00:38,02
State management is the implementation of a design pattern

18
00:00:38,02 --> 00:00:40,07
to synchronize the state of your application

19
00:00:40,07 --> 00:00:43,07
throughout all the components of your application.

20
00:00:43,07 --> 00:00:46,02
Indeed, application state management is crucial

21
00:00:46,02 --> 00:00:48,02
in software developments.

22
00:00:48,02 --> 00:00:51,01
And as your applications grows in size and complexity,

23
00:00:51,01 --> 00:00:53,01
it is time to think beyond the basics.

24
00:00:53,01 --> 00:00:55,07
And learning to manage the state effectively becomes

25
00:00:55,07 --> 00:00:57,09
critical for every project.

26
00:00:57,09 --> 00:00:59,04
For any development team,

27
00:00:59,04 --> 00:01:02,01
the goal is to pick the right state management solution

28
00:01:02,01 --> 00:01:04,08
and the techniques that works for your needs.

29
00:01:04,08 --> 00:01:07,05
And this is what makes the difference between clean code

30
00:01:07,05 --> 00:01:10,05
and code which is difficult to maintain and understand,

31
00:01:10,05 --> 00:01:13,07
infamously known as spaghetti code.

32
00:01:13,07 --> 00:01:16,00
And so effective state management is key

33
00:01:16,00 --> 00:01:19,01
for building robust and maintainable software systems.

34
00:01:19,01 --> 00:01:21,01
And understanding how to effectively manage

35
00:01:21,01 --> 00:01:23,05
the state of your application is essential

36
00:01:23,05 --> 00:01:26,06
to software and web development.

37
00:01:26,06 --> 00:01:29,06
This course is not just about teaching state management,

38
00:01:29,06 --> 00:01:32,06
but also to show how to choose the right solution

39
00:01:32,06 --> 00:01:34,08
and help you build large-scale applications

40
00:01:34,08 --> 00:01:37,04
that are quality-driven, highly maintainable,

41
00:01:37,04 --> 00:01:39,00
easy to test and to scale.

